<Post title="Guaranteed delivery: Lean verification" description="Exact theorem domains, remaining proof obligations and reproducible Lean sources." updated="2026-10-25">
  <p><a href="/cop-prisoner/">Overview</a> · <a href="/cop-prisoner/#resources">Resources</a> · <a href="/cop-prisoner/proofs/">Classification proofs</a> · <a href="/cop-prisoner/delivery-time/">Delivery-time companion</a></p>
  <p><strong>The ordinary classification is complete; full Lean verification is in progress.</strong> The mathematical answer gives the exact maximum and an explicit attaining graph for every admissible pair. The accepted formal development now covers the complete construction side and substantial exact upper-bound domains. It has not yet proved the full universal maximum theorem.</p>
  <h2>Current accepted results</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Every prescribed graph and its claimed score.</strong> For every admissible <Math tex={String.raw`(n,m)`} />, Lean verifies the specified graph's looplessness, exact arrow count and exact claimed score. Universal optimality additionally requires excluding better competing graphs.</li>
    <li><strong>The complete large-order classification.</strong> For every <Math tex={String.raw`n\ge12`} /> and admissible <Math tex={String.raw`m\ge24`} />, the maximum and an explicit attaining graph are verified. All finite main-interval and sparse-construction bridges are closed.</li>
    <li><strong>Sharp unrestricted small budgets.</strong> Budgets 0–14 and 22 have their sharp upper bounds over arbitrary finite hosts, including sources, sinks and isolates. These bounds have matching prescribed graphs at the stated support orders.</li>
    <li><strong>Small hosts.</strong> Every budget at orders through six is verified. The seven-vertex budgets 18–42 and eight-vertex budgets 24–56 also have proved upper bounds and attaining graphs. The latest additional cell is <Math tex={String.raw`M(7,18)=14`} />.</li>
    <li><strong>Further complete domains.</strong> The dense classification from order eleven, the functional endpoint at every order from two, the full zero band and all fifteen designated smaller dense exceptions remain verified, together with the previously stated stronger subset and delivery-time guarantees.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These are accepted development results newer than the downloadable snapshot below. The current source development uses Lean 4.33.1 and kernel checking. No external solver assertion, custom axiom, proof hole or native proof is accepted; reported logical axioms are confined to <code>propext</code>, <code>Classical.choice</code> and <code>Quot.sound</code>.</p>
  <h2>Exactly what remains</h2>
  <p><strong>Eight sharp global budgets remain:</strong> 15–21 and 23. There are also <strong>25 separate fixed-host upper exclusions</strong>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Seven vertices: 14–17 arrows.</li>
    <li>Eight vertices: 17–23 arrows.</li>
    <li>Nine vertices: 17 and 19–23 arrows.</li>
    <li>Ten vertices: 19 and 21–24 arrows.</li>
    <li>Eleven vertices: 21, 23 and 24 arrows.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>After these bounds, the final quantified maximum theorem and complete source-release reconciliation remain. Every graph and its claimed score are already verified; these outstanding obligations concern competing graphs. They are formal-proof gaps, not unknown numerical values.</p>
  <p>At the 25 October 2026, 06:40 UTC development checkpoint, all 80 hard positive degree families of the fifteen-arrow, eight-vertex component, their complete catalogue membership, and the normalized support-eight assembly are accepted. The normalization assumes every vertex has total degree at least two and is positive in both directions or has total degree two. This proves the stated component upper bound of fifteen; the unrestricted fifteen-arrow theorem remains unfinished. Separately, an independent route to the sharp twenty-arrow bound has prior-free weak bounds of 36, 44 and 53 at budgets 16, 18 and 19, and three of its sixteen target-family exclusions accepted; thirteen remain. Those weaker bounds do not close the sharp earlier budgets.</p>
  <h2>Downloadable verified snapshot</h2>
  <p>The existing <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean-proofs.zip">Lean source archive</a> and <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean-verification.json">verification receipt</a> identify the earlier released snapshot, dated {release.artifact_snapshots.lean.date}. Its {verification.modules.length} distributed modules passed the recorded replay. Newer development claims above do not extend that archive's recorded scope. The module count is an inventory, not a completion percentage.</p>
  <p>Extract the archive, install its pinned Lean 4.33.1 toolchain and run <code>python3 check.py</code> inside the extracted <code>lean</code> folder. Its receipt pins source hashes, compiler, successful checks and logical axioms. The <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/README.md">released theorem guide</a> describes that snapshot's precise statements.</p>
  <details>
    <summary>Detailed theorem map and proof limits of the earlier downloadable snapshot</summary>
    <p>The statements and outstanding obligations in this section describe that release. The current development's stronger domains and remaining obligations are listed above.</p>
  <h2>Exact maxima and explicit constructions already verified</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>The uniform sparse construction from support order 85.</strong> For every <Math tex={String.raw`n\ge k\ge85`} />, Lean proves <Math tex={String.raw`M(n,2k)=k(k-3)`} />. The literal six-type cyclic graph, its local projection, all 552 strategy objectives in 81 covered patterns, global strategy composition, exact counts, and isolate padding are connected. Supports 12–18, 50, 55, 65, 70, 75 and 80 also follow from the finite main endpoints below. The remaining even bridge is stated explicitly at the end of this page. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/SixTypeConstruction.lean">SixTypeConstruction</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Uniform odd sparse maxima from support order 98.</strong> For every <Math tex={String.raw`n\ge s\ge98`} />, Lean proves <Math tex={String.raw`M(n,2s-1)=(s-1)(s-4)+2`} />. All 124 local patterns and 847 objectives, actual cyclic geometry, every cop reply, global safe transfer and exact counts are supplied. The same catalogue also covers supports 88, 89, 90, 94, 95 and 96. Six retained graphs cover supports 13–18. All pad to every larger host. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/OddEndpointConstruction.lean">Uniform construction</a>, <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/OddEndpointFiniteCorollaries.lean">earlier residue cases</a>, and <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/SmallOddConstruction.lean">small supports</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>The complete main interval at every order from 115.</strong> For every <Math tex={String.raw`n\ge115`} /> and <Math tex={String.raw`2n\le m\le n(n-3)`} />, Lean proves <Math tex={String.raw`M(n,m)=n(n-1)-m`} /> with explicit attaining graphs. All 101 local patterns and 696 objectives, actual optional cop replies, safe-transfer composition, exact counts and prescribed optional-prefix budgets are supplied. The lower construction also retains its larger envelope endpoint. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/LowBandConstruction.lean">LowBandConstruction</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>The upper main interval at every order from 25.</strong> Every <Math tex={String.raw`3n\le m\le n(n-3)`} /> attains all missing pairs. Counted circle, hub and separated-code recipes have prescribed parameters and proved overlaps. At orders 19, 20, 21, 22, 23 and 24 the same assembly respectively covers budgets 95–304, 100–340, 126–378, 110–418, 115–460 and 120–504. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/MainUpperInterval.lean">MainUpperInterval</a>. The separate pair-code family retains two-move delivery for every optional subset.</li>
    <li><strong>Complete main intervals at every order 12–18.</strong> Thirty saved rank envelopes supply order twelve, and 145 further stages cover orders thirteen through eighteen, with a pair-code endpoint. Each stage checks all initial cop positions, waiting, optional cop arrows and exact arrow counts. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/MainTwelve.lean">MainTwelve</a> and <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/MainSmallClassification.lean">MainSmallClassification</a>. Their endpoints also give the even sparse maxima on supports 12–18, padded to every larger host.</li>
    <li><strong>Ten further complete main intervals and two short intervals.</strong> The five-type constructions prove the entire main interval at orders 65, 70, 75, 80, 85, 90, 95, 100, 105 and 110. The short charts cover budgets 100–110 at order 50 and 110–121 at order 55. Each has an exact optional-prefix recipe. Their endpoints give even sparse maxima on all twelve supports and every larger host. The proof transports common-envelope symmetries without assuming that a selected optional graph is symmetric. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/FiveTypeClassification.lean">FiveTypeClassification</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>The complete dense range for every <Math tex={String.raw`n\ge11`} />.</strong> For <Math tex={String.raw`n(n-3)\le m\le n(n-1)`} />, Lean proves the exact maximum and a concrete attaining graph. At <Math tex={String.raw`m=n(n-3)`} /> the value is <Math tex={String.raw`2n`} />; for <Math tex={String.raw`r=m-n(n-3)`} /> with <Math tex={String.raw`1\le r\le n`} />, it is <Math tex={String.raw`2n-r-\lceil r/2\rceil-1`} />; above <Math tex={String.raw`n(n-2)`} /> it is zero. Arbitrary-graph upper bounds, root and core constructions, exact counts and every threshold case are supplied. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/DenseSharpClassification.lean">DenseSharpClassification</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>The adjacent band for every <Math tex={String.raw`n \ge  16`} />.</strong> For <Math tex={String.raw`n(n - 4) \le  m \le  n(n - 3)`} />, the maximum equals the number of missing pairs, <Math tex={String.raw`n(n - 1) - m`} />. Explicit even and odd formulas and finite repairs cover every order in this domain. Every optional subset works within two moves; taking the first required optional arrows gives the exact budget. Together with the preceding result, this verifies every budget <Math tex={String.raw`m \ge  n(n - 4)`} /> when <Math tex={String.raw`n \ge  16`} />. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/DenseEnvelopeClassification.lean">DenseEnvelopeClassification</a>.</li>
