  </ol>
  <h2>Complete small budgets and small host tables</h2>
  <p>The unrestricted sharp upper bounds at budgets 0–10 are 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2, 4, 5 and 6. Matching graphs are proved at every admissible host for 0–3, from host four for 4–6, from five for 7–8, and from six for 9–10. Sources, sinks and isolates are included. Complete degree-profile and row-choice coverage accompanies every finite exclusion. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/SmallBudgetTen.lean">The ten-arrow theorem</a> completes this chain.</p>
  <p>Every admissible budget at every order at most five is classified, with explicit attainers. The four-vertex proof covers all loopless adjacency choices. The five-vertex proof combines actual source/sink deletion, a complete positive-degree catalogue and seven retained witnesses. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/TinyOrderClassification.lean">Orders zero to three</a>, <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/FourVertexClassification.lean">order four</a>, and <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/FiveVertexClassification.lean">order five</a>.</p>
  <h2>General bounds and finite exclusions</h2>
  <p><a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/VertexBound.lean">VertexBound</a> proves <Math tex={String.raw`I(G) \le  n(n - 3)`} /> for every loopless graph with <Math tex={String.raw`n \ge  3`} />. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/SparseParity.lean">SparseParity</a> proves the unrestricted budget bounds <Math tex={String.raw`I(G) \le  k(k - 3)`} /> for <Math tex={String.raw`2k`} /> arrows and <Math tex={String.raw`I(G) \le  k(k - 3) + 2`} /> for <Math tex={String.raw`2k + 1`} /> arrows, for every <Math tex={String.raw`k \ge  5`} />. Support counting, deletion, strategy preservation and induction are discharged; the small auxiliary induction bounds are not the sharp finite table.</p>
  <p><a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/FiniteExclusionUnrestrictedNine.lean">The complete nine-vertex strictness proof</a> establishes <Math tex={String.raw`I(G) \le  53`} /> for every loopless nine-vertex graph. It includes degree rigidity, matching factorization, canonical permutation cycles and all eight complete exclusion trees. This strictness result alone does not prove all nine-vertex maxima. Further checked interfaces support optimistic partial-game pruning and symmetry reductions; additional exclusion families still require complete concrete certificates.</p>
  <p><a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/RegularNineSharp.lean">The sharp regular-nine exclusion</a> proves exact maximum <Math tex={String.raw`30`} /> among all loopless nine-vertex graphs with two incoming and two outgoing arrows at each vertex. Factorization, normalization, all eight first-factor cycle types, complete exclusion trees and an explicit attainer are included. This restricted-family maximum does not establish the unrestricted eighteen-arrow value of 33.</p>
  <p>Signed winning and losing certificates verify the exact scores 8, 9, 11, 13, 15, 19, 28, 33, 40, 53, 60, 79 and 83 of retained graphs at budgets 11–23, respectively. All their supports have at most twelve vertices; each graph pads to every larger host. These are lower witnesses, and do not by themselves prove an upper bound over all competing graphs. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/SmallSparseWitnesses.lean">The witness and padding assembly</a> states every support and score. Earlier literal witnesses remain available.</p>
  <p><a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/PositiveFourteenIsolates.lean">The sharp fourteen-arrow positive-support exclusion</a> proves score at most thirteen whenever the nonisolated support has at least nine vertices and every supported vertex has positive incoming and outgoing degree. Arbitrary isolates are allowed. The nine-vertex proof covers all eleven normalized joint profiles and 160,718 proof-DAG nodes; the ten-vertex proof and larger-support counting complete the stated range. Smaller supports and sources/sinks remain separate obligations for the unrestricted fourteen-arrow maximum.</p>
  <h2>The actual game and the trust boundary</h2>
  <p>Both players may wait; the messenger moves first and receipt precedes collision. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/SemanticCompleteness.lean">SemanticCompleteness</a> proves equivalence between finite winning trees and one fixed messenger policy that eventually delivers against every permitted initial cop and every legal history-dependent cop policy. No time bound is assumed in the actual-play definition.</p>
  <p><a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/GraphPadding.lean">Padding</a> preserves scores exactly when adding isolates or sinks with at most one predecessor, including cops starting at or entering the new sink. <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/LocalArena.lean">LocalArena</a> proves projection and sequential composition for separate messenger/cop state spaces. A safe transfer includes the cop reply before the next stage; only terminal receipt waives collision at the recipient. Concrete geometry and certificate premises remain visible until instantiated.</p>
  <p>All finite checks use Lean kernel reduction. No external solver assertion, custom axiom, proof hole or native proof is accepted. Reported axioms are confined to Lean's standard <code>propext</code>, <code>Classical.choice</code> and <code>Quot.sound</code>. Certificate producers are untrusted and unnecessary for replaying the literal distributed sources.</p>
